WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.650
We've all heard the saying, "food is love",

2
00:00:02.650 --> 00:00:06.620
but for Latrice MacArthur, it holds especially true.

3
00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:09.770
She's a chef and a teacher and the founder of

4
00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:12.680
Wellness with Bella, an afterschool program

5
00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:15.960
focused on healthy eating and meals for those in need.

6
00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:18.187
Please welcome Latrice.

7
00:00:18.187 --> 00:00:21.060
(audience applause)

8
00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:21.893
Hello!

9
00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:26.080
Hi, nice to meet you.

10
00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:29.240
Oh my gosh, you look so beautiful.

11
00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:32.110
You look great, as usual.

12
00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:32.943
Oh, thank you.

13
00:00:32.943 --> 00:00:35.850
This is a ton of hair, makeup and wardrobe, trust me.

14
00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:39.840
And I was curious what inspired you

15
00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:43.910
to jump into community action and start your program.

16
00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:45.940
So a little over 10 years ago,

17
00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:48.240 line:15%
when the former first lady Michelle Obama

18
00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:50.420 line:15%
started her, Let's Move initiative,

19
00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:52.340 line:15%
and she asked for chefs to come in

20
00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:54.680 line:15%
and volunteer in elementary schools.

21
00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:57.490 line:15%
And I was working as a private chef at that time,

22
00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.080 line:15%
and decided sure I can go in

23
00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:01.230 line:15%
and the anticipated volunteering,

24
00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:04.090 line:15%
maybe a day or two, possibly a week.

25
00:01:04.090 --> 00:01:06.520 line:15%
But after spending time with the kids,

26
00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:10.090
I saw a tremendous need to be able to educate them

27
00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:13.920
on food, and nutrition, and culinary skills, as well.

28
00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:17.770
And within a year, the nonprofit was started.

29
00:01:17.770 --> 00:01:21.010
And you discovered during the pandemic,

30
00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:24.033
like a new sense of purpose, will you tell us about that?

31
00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:26.420
Absolutely.

32
00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:29.520 line:15%
So initially, when we got the call that schools

33
00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:30.370 line:15%
were gonna be closed.

34
00:01:30.370 --> 00:01:32.190 line:15%
Just like everyone else, we anticipated

35
00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:34.370 line:15%
that it would only be for two weeks.

36
00:01:34.370 --> 00:01:36.360 line:15%
And then we said, sure, we can figure that out,

37
00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:39.300
and get out a couple of hundred meals.

38
00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:42.180
And so I pulled together our volunteers,

39
00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:44.360
and then we figured out how to deliver.

40
00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:46.750
And that couple of hundred meals that we anticipated

41
00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:50.212
has turned into now, 15,000 meals that we have been able

42
00:01:50.212 --> 00:01:51.956
to deliver.

43
00:01:51.956 --> 00:01:54.725
Oh my goodness!
(audience applause)

44
00:01:54.725 --> 00:01:55.713
I mean, Latrice!

45
00:01:56.590 --> 00:02:00.410
You are the angel that we all hope exists on the planet,

46
00:02:00.410 --> 00:02:03.510
because when we all watched what happened at the beginning

47
00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:07.970
of school closures, it was so heartbreaking, so scary.

48
00:02:07.970 --> 00:02:10.110
And even on your website,

49
00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:12.950
the mission statement says, change a life today.

50
00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:16.310
And that's so simple and so impactful,

51
00:02:16.310 --> 00:02:18.170
and that's exactly what you're doing,

52
00:02:18.170 --> 00:02:21.143
but over and over and over again.

53
00:02:22.630 --> 00:02:24.606
You know, and it seems so simplistic.

54
00:02:24.606 --> 00:02:26.530
It doesn't seem like it should be an issue,

55
00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:28.600 line:15%
but hunger is a huge issue.

56
00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:31.420 line:15%
And, you know, we can't expect our children to go to school

57
00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:33.280 line:15%
and be able to function, and thrive

58
00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:35.540 line:15%
if they have not had a proper meal.

59
00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:38.260
And so this is my mission to make sure that

60
00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:40.480
not only are we providing the meals as far as students,

61
00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:44.530
but also making sure that they are ready to thrive in school

62
00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:47.470
to be able to close some of those success and education gaps

63
00:02:47.470 --> 00:02:50.200
that exists in these communities.

64
00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:54.270
Well, thank goodness for you Latrice.

65
00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:59.150
And I heard that you're a big admirer of Anne Burrell.

66
00:02:59.150 --> 00:02:59.983
Is that true?

67
00:03:00.932 --> 00:03:02.540
That is so true.

68
00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:05.380
I love her, by the way, obsessed.

69
00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:06.213
I love her.

70
00:03:06.213 --> 00:03:09.620
I love her style, I love the way she, her recipes,

71
00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:11.240
the way she brought us into the kitchen.

72
00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:12.720
I really adore her.

73
00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:14.660
Oh, well that's good cause she adores you too.

74
00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:16.757
Guess who's here? It's Anne Burrell.

75
00:03:16.757 --> 00:03:19.277
(audience applause)

76
00:03:19.277 --> 00:03:22.110
(women squealing)

77
00:03:24.074 --> 00:03:25.909
Oh my gosh.

78
00:03:25.909 --> 00:03:27.877
Oh my gosh, look how,

79
00:03:29.097 --> 00:03:30.570
How cute are you?

80
00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:34.023
And that smile is just infectious.

81
00:03:35.487 --> 00:03:36.630
Oh, and hi Drew!

82
00:03:36.630 --> 00:03:37.463
Hi Anne.

83
00:03:37.463 --> 00:03:39.630
When I heard about you, Latrice,

84
00:03:39.630 --> 00:03:43.290 line:15%
and all of the wonderful stuff that you do,

85
00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:47.756 line:15%
for so many people, it actually makes me weepy.

86
00:03:47.756 --> 00:03:51.160
I'm a huge fan of Chicago and I go there kind of regularly.

87
00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:53.000
So I feel like the next time I'm in town,

88
00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:54.660
I'm gonna like swing by, and maybe

89
00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:57.040
I'll help you cook for a day or something.

90
00:03:57.040 --> 00:03:58.640
Yes!
And I would love that.

91
00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:03.803
Not again, to be a weirdo, but I want in on that.

92
00:04:04.865 --> 00:04:05.698
Okay.

93
00:04:05.698 --> 00:04:10.698
And we at the show wanted to donate to your mission,

94
00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:12.670
and to the families in Chicago.

95
00:04:12.670 --> 00:04:14.310
So our friends at Trifecta,

96
00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:16.700
an organic meal delivery service,

97
00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:20.720
are giving you 500 meals to distribute

98
00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:22.313
throughout your community.

99
00:04:22.313 --> 00:04:23.254
(audience applause)

100
00:04:23.254 --> 00:04:26.957
And I thank them so much for that.

101
00:04:26.957 --> 00:04:30.560
That's fantastic, thank you so much!

102
00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:33.490
Oh, that's gonna help so many kids, thank you!

103
00:04:33.490 --> 00:04:35.270
It's not enough, but it's a start.

104
00:04:35.270 --> 00:04:39.790
And Anne, did you want to add anything to that?

105
00:04:39.790 --> 00:04:44.410
Well, Latrice, everything that you do is so important.

106
00:04:44.410 --> 00:04:47.663
So the people at Trifecta want to give you 500 more meals!

107
00:04:49.707 --> 00:04:51.457
So that's 1000 meals.

108
00:04:53.063 --> 00:04:55.930
Oh my God.
(audience applause)

109
00:04:55.930 --> 00:04:59.550
I mean, all the work that you do is so important

110
00:04:59.550 --> 00:05:03.264
and we just wanna keep that smile as bright,

111
00:05:03.264 --> 00:05:07.250
as electric, as it absolutely is.

112
00:05:07.250 --> 00:05:09.980
Absolutely.
Thank you guys, so much.

113
00:05:09.980 --> 00:05:11.330
Oh, this is amazing.

114
00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:13.287
Our kids are gonna love this, thank you.

115
00:05:13.287 --> 00:05:16.790
Thank you to Trifecta for helping us, do this.

116
00:05:16.790 --> 00:05:19.570
And Anne Burrell, I love you so much,

117
00:05:19.570 --> 00:05:21.851
I can't believe I'm gonna do this with you.

118
00:05:21.851 --> 00:05:24.280
I see you Drew Barrymore, I love you.

119
00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:28.010 line:15%
Latrice, I mean, you are just a rock star

120
00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:31.200 line:15%
and thank you guys so much for including me in this.

121
00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:32.410
Aww.

122
00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:33.243
Yes.

123
00:05:33.243 --> 00:05:34.076
Thank you both.

124
00:05:34.076 --> 00:05:36.296
Your blessing is so exciting, thank you.

125
00:05:36.296 --> 00:05:38.350
Oh Latrice and Anne.

126
00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:40.530
Oh, be sure to check out the new season

127
00:05:40.530 --> 00:05:42.350
of Worst Cooks in America.

128
00:05:42.350 --> 00:05:45.040
Premiering April 25th at 9:00 PM,

129
00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:47.978
8:00 PM central on the Food Network.

130
00:05:47.978 --> 00:05:50.561
(upbeat music)

